{"book":{"id":"book-rebel-land-among-turkey-s-forgotten-peoples-christopher-de-bellaigue","slug":"rebel-land-among-turkey-s-forgotten-peoples-christopher-de-bellaigue","title":"Rebel Land: Among Turkey's Forgotten Peoples","authors":[{"id":"person-christopher-de-bellaigue","name":"Christopher de Bellaigue"}],"isbn13":["9780747586289"],"subjects":["Travel & Place"],"topics":["Genocide, Atrocity & Political Violence","Death, Memory & Commemoration","Empire & Colonialism","Food, Agriculture & Land"],"centralFigures":[],"links":{"amazon":"https://www.amazon.com/s?k=Rebel%20Land%3A%20Among%20Turkey's%20Forgotten%20Peoples%20Christopher%20de%20Bellaigue","bookshop":"https://bookshop.org/search?keywords=Rebel%20Land%3A%20Among%20Turkey's%20Forgotten%20Peoples%20Christopher%20de%20Bellaigue","indiebound":"https://www.indiebound.org/search/book?keys=Rebel%20Land%3A%20Among%20Turkey's%20Forgotten%20Peoples%20Christopher%20de%20Bellaigue","worldcat":"https://search.worldcat.org/search?q=Rebel%20Land%3A%20Among%20Turkey's%20Forgotten%20Peoples%20Christopher%20de%20Bellaigue","publisher":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL13633396W"},"sourceIds":["source-award-record-orwell-combined-book-wikipedia-orwell-prize","source-open-library-rebel-land-among-turkey-s-forgotten-peoples-christopher-de-bellaigue","source-open-library-summary-rebel-land-among-turkey-s-forgotten-peoples-christopher-de-bellaigue"],"publicationYear":2009,"thumbnailUrl":"https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/11485568-L.jpg","readerProfile":{"readerLevel":"crossover","narrativeScore":0,"accessibilityScore":0,"scholarlyScore":0,"traits":[{"id":"essayistic","score":1,"confidence":"high","evidence":["catalog text contains \"essay\"","catalog text contains \"essays\"","catalog text contains \"criticism\"","literature/criticism subject or topic"]}],"method":"deterministic_catalog_heuristics_v1"},"renownProfile":{"knowsBook":true,"publicFame":34,"criticalRenown":59,"controversy":43,"llmAffinity":84,"affinityResidual":8.43,"confidence":{"publicFame":0.86,"criticalRenown":0.82,"controversy":0.72,"llmAffinity":0.95},"tags":{"craft":"prose-style","evidence":"reportage","stance":"revisionism"},"model":"gpt-5.6-luna","promptVersion":1},"summary":"An esteemed journalist travels to Turkey to investigate the legacy of the Armenian genocide and the quest for Kurdish statehood. In 2001, Christopher de Bellaigue, then the Economist's correspondent in Istanbul, wrote a piece about the history of Turkey for The New York Review of Books. In it, he briefly discussed the killing and deportation of half a million Armenians in 1915. These massacres, he suggested, were best understood as part of the struggles that attended the end of the Ottoman empire.After the story was published, the magazine was besieged with letters. This wasn't war, the correspondents said; it was genocide. And the death toll was not half a million but three times that many. De Bellaigue was mortified. How had he gotten it so wrong? He went back to Turkey, but found that the national archives had sealed all documents pertaining to those times. Undeterred and armed with a stack of contraband histories, he set out to the conflicted southeastern Turkish city of Varto to discover what had really happened.There, de Bellaigue found a place in which the centuries-old conflict among Turks, Armenians, and Kurds was still very much alive.","subjectCategories":[{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"History","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-rebel-land-among-turkey-s-forgotten-peoples-christopher-de-bellaigue"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Nonfiction","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-rebel-land-among-turkey-s-forgotten-peoples-christopher-de-bellaigue"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Social life and customs","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-rebel-land-among-turkey-s-forgotten-peoples-christopher-de-bellaigue"},{"source":"open